IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er4-nouns`
IMPORT `er4-part3-qualifying-plan`

-- Tests of reg 67 (SOR-96-332.txt lines 1109-1124). Every expected value is written by hand from the text.

§ `Reg 67(1) -- a formal written commitment`

#ASSERT `reg 67(1) the plan is evidenced by a formal written commitment` (LIST `er4 a union or association agreement`)
#ASSERT `reg 67(1) the plan is evidenced by a formal written commitment` (LIST `er4 a private carrier insurance policy`, `er4 an industry-wide plan`)
#ASSERT `reg 67(1) the plan is evidenced by a formal written commitment` (LIST `er4 another formal written commitment`)
-- Nothing in writing: not evidenced.
#ASSERT NOT `reg 67(1) the plan is evidenced by a formal written commitment` EMPTY
-- A board of directors' resolution counts only if "implemented", alone or in combination.
#ASSERT `reg 67(1) the plan is evidenced by a formal written commitment` (LIST `er4 a board of directors' resolution` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `reg 67(1) the plan is evidenced by a formal written commitment` (LIST `er4 a board of directors' resolution` FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 67(1) the plan is evidenced by a formal written commitment` (LIST `er4 a board of directors' resolution` FALSE, `er4 an undertaking contained in an employees' handbook`)

§ `Reg 67(4) -- the 15th day of the month`

-- On or before the 15th: the first day of that month. After the 15th: the first day of the following month.
#ASSERT `reg 67(4) the day on which a plan is considered to become or cease to be a qualifying plan` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1
#ASSERT `reg 67(4) the day on which a plan is considered to become or cease to be a qualifying plan` (YMD 2026 3 15) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1
#ASSERT `reg 67(4) the day on which a plan is considered to become or cease to be a qualifying plan` (YMD 2026 3 16) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 1
#ASSERT `reg 67(4) the day on which a plan is considered to become or cease to be a qualifying plan` (YMD 2026 1 31) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 1
#ASSERT `reg 67(4) the day on which a plan is considered to become or cease to be a qualifying plan` (YMD 2026 12 16) EQUALS YMD 2027 1 1

§ `Reg 67(5) -- plans of section 65 or 66 credited with 72 or 120 days minus the days that could have accumulated`

#ASSERT `reg 67(5)(a) the days of paid sick leave a person must be credited with under a plan of section 65` 20 EQUALS 52
#ASSERT `reg 67(5)(b) the days of paid sick leave a person must be credited with under a plan of section 66` 20 EQUALS 100
-- Section 65 plan: 72 - 20 = 52 and 72 - 2 = 70.
#ASSERT `reg 67(5) each insured person covered by the plan is credited with the days the subsection requires` `er4 a Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan` (LIST (`er4 Credit of an insured person covered by a plan` OF 52, 20), (`er4 Credit of an insured person covered by a plan` OF 70, 2)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- One person credited 51 instead of 52: not met.
#ASSERT `reg 67(5) each insured person covered by the plan is credited with the days the subsection requires` `er4 a Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan` (LIST (`er4 Credit of an insured person covered by a plan` OF 52, 20), (`er4 Credit of an insured person covered by a plan` OF 69, 2)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "Equal to": credited with MORE than the figure is not met either.
#ASSERT `reg 67(5) each insured person covered by the plan is credited with the days the subsection requires` `er4 a Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan` (LIST (`er4 Credit of an insured person covered by a plan` OF 53, 20)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Section 66 plan: 120 - 20 = 100.
#ASSERT `reg 67(5) each insured person covered by the plan is credited with the days the subsection requires` `er4 an Enhanced Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan` (LIST (`er4 Credit of an insured person covered by a plan` OF 100, 20)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 67(5) each insured person covered by the plan is credited with the days the subsection requires` `er4 an Enhanced Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan` (LIST (`er4 Credit of an insured person covered by a plan` OF 52, 20)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A plan of section 63 or 64 is not "referred to in section 65 or 66": not covered by (5).
#ASSERT `reg 67(5) each insured person covered by the plan is credited with the days the subsection requires` `er4 a Weekly Indemnity Plan` EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING
-- The day: the later of the application and the day under (4), when credited.
#ASSERT `reg 67(5) the day as of which the plan is considered to be a qualifying plan` (YMD 2026 3 10) (YMD 2026 4 1) TRUE EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 4 1)
#ASSERT `reg 67(5) the day as of which the plan is considered to be a qualifying plan` (YMD 2026 5 10) (YMD 2026 4 1) TRUE EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 5 10)
#ASSERT `reg 67(5) the day as of which the plan is considered to be a qualifying plan` (YMD 2026 5 10) (YMD 2026 4 1) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Reg 67(3) -- the qualifying plan`

-- Arguments: kind, evidenced, meets the requirements of the section for its kind, credited as (5) requires.
#ASSERT `reg 67(3) the plan is a qualifying plan` `er4 a Weekly Indemnity Plan` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 67(3) the plan is a qualifying plan` `er4 a Special Weekly Indemnity Plan` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 67(3) the plan is a qualifying plan` `er4 a Weekly Indemnity Plan` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 67(3) the plan is a qualifying plan` `er4 a Weekly Indemnity Plan` TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- Subject to (5) for a plan of section 65 or 66.
#ASSERT `reg 67(3) the plan is a qualifying plan` `er4 a Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 67(3) the plan is a qualifying plan` `er4 a Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 67(3) the plan is a qualifying plan` `er4 an Enhanced Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 67(3) the plan is a qualifying plan` `er4 an Enhanced Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- A plan of none of the four kinds cannot meet any of the four sections.
#ASSERT NOT `reg 67(3) the plan is a qualifying plan` `er4 another wage-loss plan` TRUE TRUE TRUE

§ `Reg 67(2) -- the number of months of the year to which the reduction applies`

-- Arguments: year, day considered to become a qualifying plan, day considered to cease (if it has), effective date under reg 71.
-- A plan qualifying for the whole of 2026: 12 months.
#ASSERT `reg 67(2) the number of months in the year to which the reduction applies` 2026 (YMD 2025 6 1) NOTHING (YMD 2025 7 1) EQUALS 12
-- Becomes a qualifying plan on 1 April 2026: April to December, 9 months.
#ASSERT `reg 67(2) the number of months in the year to which the reduction applies` 2026 (YMD 2026 4 1) NOTHING (YMD 2026 4 1) EQUALS 9
-- And ceases on 1 October 2026: April to September, 6 months.
#ASSERT `reg 67(2) the number of months in the year to which the reduction applies` 2026 (YMD 2026 4 1) (JUST (YMD 2026 10 1)) (YMD 2026 4 1) EQUALS 6
-- A later effective date under reg 71 (1 May): May to December, 8 months.
#ASSERT `reg 67(2) the number of months in the year to which the reduction applies` 2026 (YMD 2026 4 1) NOTHING (YMD 2026 5 1) EQUALS 8
-- Ceased before the year began: none.
#ASSERT `reg 67(2) the number of months in the year to which the reduction applies` 2026 (YMD 2025 1 1) (JUST (YMD 2025 12 1)) (YMD 2025 2 1) EQUALS 0
-- Ceased on 1 January 2026: the first month of 2026 is not one in which it was a qualifying plan.
#ASSERT `reg 67(2) the number of months in the year to which the reduction applies` 2026 (YMD 2025 1 1) (JUST (YMD 2026 1 1)) (YMD 2025 2 1) EQUALS 0
